  "$note_on_the_2026_09_10_jump": "34 -> 60. NOT a regression: no definition was added, the guard was fixed. Its CREATE TABLE pattern required a bare word after the optional IF NOT EXISTS, so a leading double quote failed the match outright — and `drizzle-kit generate` quotes everything. `migrations/0000_sweet_joseph.sql`, the drizzle baseline, holds 297 CREATE TABLE statements, sits in the root migrations/ tree that install-fresh’s overlay walks, and was counted by this guard as creating NOTHING. Distinct tables seen went 1150 -> 1416. 31 entries below name that file; 26 are collisions the guard could not previously see. Proved by making it fail: with the old pattern, and a probe file adding a QUOTED second definition of q_submissions, the guard scanned 586 files and reported \"34 defined more than once\" and a green tick. The shrink rule still holds — from 60. Resolving these is WO-1 stages 2–4; the cortex.* entries are parked pending WO-14."
